cartridge "PEGS/COMPUTE'S GAZETTE/1986"

' PEGS
' A ColecoVision game based on "Pegs", COMPUTE!'s Gazette, December 1986
' (issue 42; Commodore 64 and VIC-20, BASIC; the listing names no
' author). Made for Amy Studio by Claude (an AI made by Anthropic), 2026,
' in Amy by Amy Bienvenu.
'
' The game (orig/pegs_64.bas, primary; orig/pegs_vic.bas is the same
' program on a narrower screen): the triangle of 15 holes lettered A to O,
' every hole filled but A at the top. A peg jumps a neighbour along a line
' of the triangle into an empty hole and the jumped peg comes off (the 18
' lines of three in the listing's DATA, both ways: 36 moves). Each jump
' scores 1 point; the game ends when no jump is left, and 13 (one peg
' left) wins: CONGRATULATIONS, YOU WON. Any jump can be taken back
' (BACKUP, the listing's "_"), one at a time down to the start, also from
' the GAME OVER prompt. A wrong move: ILLEGAL MOVE and a buzz.
'
' Kept from the listing: the board and its letters, the start hole, the
' move table, the score (S, jumps made), the end test (no jump left,
' lines 260-290), 13 to win, unlimited backup (lines 340-370, the board
' of every turn: here the list of jumps made), the screens' words.
'
' Liberties:
' - The joystick replaces typing two letters: the stick moves a cursor
'   from hole to hole (the 8 directions: the nearest hole that way), the
'   left button picks a peg and then drops it on the hole to jump to;
'   the right button backs up. Picking the picked peg again puts it down;
'   picking another peg changes the choice.
' - A move is checked when it is made: picking an empty hole, or a jump
'   that is not one of the 36, says ILLEGAL MOVE (the listing checked the
'   typed pair the same way).
' - The win's border flashes slowly (the original cycled all 16 colours
'   20 times in about a second).
' - At GAME OVER the left button ends the game (the listing's N) and the
'   right button backs up; there is no PLAY AGAIN: the game goes back to
'   the title. The title keeps the best score; the play screen also
'   shows the pegs left and what the buttons do.
' - The look is new: a green felt triangle, gold pegs carrying their
'   letters, white when picked, black holes that keep their letter, the
'   peg hopping over in an arc. Sounds and the title tune ("Jump the
'   Row") are new.
'
' Controls: either controller; stick and side buttons only (no keypad).
'
' House rules: text in columns 2-29, rows 1-22; tiles from code 128;
' frame loop protected from the NMI; screens drawn with the NMI and the
' display off. Music first in the sound table, the title tune once.

